{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/676037-car-smack-issue","id":676037,"title":"Car Smack Issue","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-23T22:27:29-07:00","id":676037,"title":"Car Smack Issue","content":"By reading the durability rules and with the way Cyclopean Strength works it seems hitting someone with a car would only add +3 damage. <br /> This seems low for crushing someone under a hummer. <br /> <br /> Also Titanic Blow ignores Sta + Lair durability at normal activation and all at low satiety. Seems to me considering that it's super rare to find any object with more than durability 4 Sta + Lair should be enough to bust through anything anyway by lair 2.<br /> <br /> Am I missing something or is this how it should be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2553-kai","name":"Kai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2553_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T03:28:38-07:00","id":676269,"title":"","content":"Hitting people with a car (superhero style, not driving) would be rather ackward, I'd imagine. Cars are also designed to crumple, and getting a good grip to lift a car without parts of it breaking off is a feat of physics in itself, plus the force of the hit is spread out over a large area. Combined with the fact you're likely adding in your Lair dots, that makes the damage feel alright - most of the damage is coming from your strength, not the use of the car as a weapon. And +3 damage is a great boost from having bare hands.<br /> <br /> There's so many concerns on the issue, that I'm not sure we can come up with a good answer. The rules are designed to handle a wide range of objects. Some will be low, some high, and we don't want to break the game by making one thing the best weapon ever created that its dumb to use anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T07:49:03-07:00","id":676379,"title":"","content":"Considering the average character has seven health and the three is automatic on top of whatever your roll? I think it works out fairly decently.<br /> <br /> As for Titanic Blow, I'll have to think on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T08:52:26-07:00","id":676431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/676037-car-smack-issue?p=676269#post676269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hitting people with a car (superhero style, not driving) would be rather ackward, I'd imagine. Cars are also designed to crumple, and getting a good grip to lift a car without parts of it breaking off is a feat of physics in itself, plus the force of the hit is spread out over a large area. Combined with the fact you're likely adding in your Lair dots, that makes the damage feel alright - most of the damage is coming from your strength, not the use of the car as a weapon. And +3 damage is a great boost from having bare hands.<br /> <br /> There's so many concerns on the issue, that I'm not sure we can come up with a good answer. The rules are designed to handle a wide range of objects. Some will be low, some high, and we don't want to break the game by making one thing the best weapon ever created that its dumb to use anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Idk, my experience has been that vehicular assault is the easiest way to deal with serious problems in game. When you optimize for it, it quickly breaks the game, provided your ST doesn't enforce upkeep on the vehicle, which I'd advise all STs to do when someone presents you with a Demolition Dirby-style character.<br /> <br /> Of course, the point of powers like Cyclopean Strength is that you're always potentially dangerous, not that you're a one-trick pony. There are more heavy objects than just cars to fling at people, and you can't argue with stapling a guy to a wall from a couple of football fields away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T09:38:03-07:00","id":677680,"title":"","content":"Yeah, don't understand the appeal of hitting someone with a car. Lamp posts and telephone poles and good sized trees can make a car stop the hard way. Much sturdier and easy to swing like a bat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T10:26:45-07:00","id":677763,"title":"","content":"It's the most sensible way of translating &quot;If you're begging for your life, why don't you ask your money to save you!?&quot; into more realistic dialogue, I find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T12:17:22-07:00","id":677849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/676037-car-smack-issue?p=677680#post677680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, don't understand the appeal of hitting someone with a car. Lamp posts and telephone poles and good sized trees can make a car stop the hard way. Much sturdier and easy to swing like a bat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a car's not bolted down or rooted into the earth. It does assume that combat is largely happening outside, though. A person should consider storage cabinets, filing cabinets, or safes when looking for improvised weapons. The odd piece of post-modern art, perhaps. With the right build, just about any Core-10 Steel monstrosity would seriously ruin someone else's day, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T14:04:58-07:00","id":677977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/676037-car-smack-issue?p=677849#post677849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a car's not bolted down or rooted into the earth. It does assume that combat is largely happening outside, though. A person should consider storage cabinets, filing cabinets, or safes when looking for improvised weapons. The odd piece of post-modern art, perhaps. With the right build, just about any Core-10 Steel monstrosity would seriously ruin someone else's day, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>True. I am assuming, and very possibly wrongly so, that anyone who can lift a car can uproot a tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 09-25-2015, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T15:40:00-07:00","id":678034,"title":"","content":"I tend to agree why use a car when with the strength to lift a car you could use a mail box, light pole, a handy tree, or manhole cover. Concrete parking barriers though would be my first choice followed closely by the steel rods holding one in place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T19:26:04-07:00","id":678403,"title":"","content":"Answer: because people do not own mail boxes, light poles, tree, or manhole covers. They own cars.<br /> <br /> But that argument's dependent on a few things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T08:24:49-07:00","id":679041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/676037-car-smack-issue?p=678403#post678403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Answer: because people do not own mail boxes, light poles, tree, or manhole covers. They own cars.<br /> <br /> But that argument's dependent on a few things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Namely, spending nearly half of your starting Merit dots on Resources and actually caring about the property rights of NPCs. Both are kind of silly, as the former is inefficient in reliably delivering combat effectiveness as a return on investment, and the latter ignores the facts that for some characters, destruction of property is a coping strategy, and that for most templates, especially those with some manner of planar travel or access to Fate magic or Mind Control, the possibility of fines or imprisonment are minor inconveniences at worst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T09:18:38-07:00","id":679123,"title":"","content":"A point so minor you can't see it with the naked eye: in 2e, Resources represent cash and assets in excess of what the character needs to pull off his or her livelihood. Most people are going to have cars without a major investment in Resources simply because they need them. <br /> <br /> There. The most inconsequential of tangents is done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T17:04:51-07:00","id":679469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/676037-car-smack-issue?p=679123#post679123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A point so minor you can't see it with the naked eye: in 2e, Resources represent cash and assets in excess of what the character needs to pull off his or her livelihood. Most people are going to have cars without a major investment in Resources simply because they need them.<br /> <br /> There. The most inconsequential of tangents is done.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're optimizing for this action, using what has been published, you'll need at least Resources 5 in order to get a Durability 5 vehicle without it adversely affecting your pocket book. You might be able to nudge the cost down a little, but it's still a significant investment for something that will need to be repaired between game sessions. And generally, it's things that adversely affect the plot, like weapons, that should be regulated through Merits. Not doing so makes the game unbalanced.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}